EXT. MOSSY STONE BRIDGE OVER A FOGGY GORGE - DAY

A humpbacked bridge, green with moss, sits across a ravine of mist. At its center, a stool carved from a single mushroom cap.

On the stool sits GRUMBLEWICK (ancient troll, belly like a boulder, a tiny abacus in his lap). Before him stand two travelers: ELOWEN THISTLEDOWN (young, herbalist's satchel) and a hooded PEDDLER named BRAMBLEKIN (stooped, bells on his cloak).

                    GRUMBLEWICK
          Toll's three coppers.

                    ELOWEN
          Three?

                    BRAMBLEKIN
          Three?

                    ELOWEN
          ^It was two last spring.

                    BRAMBLEKIN
          ^It was two last spring.

Grumblewick flicks a bead on his abacus.

                    GRUMBLEWICK
          Inflation.

                    ELOWEN
          We can pay.

                    GRUMBLEWICK
          Then do.

Elowen counts out coins. Bramblekin watches the fog.

                    BRAMBLEKIN
          Ever think about crossing yourself?

                    GRUMBLEWICK
          Every day.

He pockets the coppers, hums a flat tune, and waves them on.
